        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(diagnostics): surface run startup phases as session-correlated events",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe embedded-agent runner reports useful startup milestones through an internal callback, but public diagnostic subscribers cannot currently observe them. That leaves status surfaces and diagnostics extensions unable to distinguish context assembly from the first model call while a turn is starting.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds the public additive diagnostic event `run.execution_phase` with the existing run/session correlation fields and the runner's phase payload. The runner entry wraps `onExecutionPhase` once, emits through the public asynchronous diagnostic lane, preserves any existing callback, and tracks session-ID rotation so later phases remain correctly correlated.\n\nThe diagnostic stability recorder and diagnostics-otel extension recognize the new event. The plugin SDK type is public like the existing run-attempt and run-progress event types. Documentation explicitly treats diagnostic event kinds as additive and tells external consumers to keep a default branch rather than assume exhaustive event-kind handling.\n\n## User Impact\n\nDiagnostics consumers can now show meaningful turn-startup progress without subscribing to an internal control-UI path. Existing callbacks and consumers retain their behavior; diagnostics-disabled processes emit nothing.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact head: `bc8abbcdb7322b80524eb18778171881703e7632`, rebased onto current `main`\n- Public `onDiagnosticEvent` regression coverage proves asynchronous delivery and ordering after earlier model events\n- Coverage proves callback forwarding, no-callback emission, diagnostics-disabled silence, and session-ID rotation\n- Canonical plugin SDK API baseline passes\n- SDK surface check is exact: 7,986 public exports (+1 type), 4,465 callable exports (unchanged), and 2,986 deprecated exports (unchanged)\n- 61 exact-head focused tests green across infra, logging, and embedded-agent diagnostics; GitHub CI is green on the exact head\n- Fresh full-branch automated review: clean (0.91 confidence)\n\nLive redacted production-path proof, emitted by `withExecutionPhaseDiagnostics` and consumed through public `onDiagnosticEvent`:\n\n```json\n[\n  {\n    \"type\": \"run.execution_phase\",\n    \"runId\": \"[redacted]\",\n    \"sessionId\": \"[redacted]\",\n    \"phase\": \"context_assembled\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"type\": \"run.execution_phase\",\n    \"runId\": \"[redacted]\",\n    \"sessionId\": \"[redacted]\",\n    \"phase\": \"model_call_started\",\n    \"firstModelCallStarted\": true\n  }\n]\n```\n\nAI-assisted (Claude/Codex, supervised): implementation, review, verification, and write-up were AI-assisted.\n",
